  "name": "sensorimotor-theory",
  "title": "Sensorimotor Contingency Theory",
  "role": "model",
  "summary": "J. Kevin O'Regan and Alva Noë hold that seeing is a way of acting: perceptual experience is the exercise of practical mastery of sensorimotor contingencies, the laws by which sensory input changes with movement. The world serves as its own outside memory, the senses differ by their laws, and the explanatory gap is said to rest on a mistaken idea of qualia.",
